# 🐛 The LaTeX numeric-extension rules above (*.[1-9] etc., a generic gitignore.io template block)
# collide with this repo's own `🏅️standards/🔖️<version>/` taxonomy dirs whenever a version looks
# like a bare digit-dot-digit ("1.2", "2.0", ...) — `🔖️1.2` ends in ".2", matching `*.[1-9]`
# exactly like a LaTeX aux file would. Found 26/08/10 (ARTIFACT-SYSTEM-OVERHAUL...) after the png
# codec's own `🔖️1.2` standard dir turned out to be silently untracked; svg's `🔖️1.1`, pdf's
# `🔖️1.4`/`🔖️1.7`, and bcf's `🔖️2.1` are the same shape. Un-ignore every `🔖️...` taxonomy dir
# explicitly rather than trying to rescope the LaTeX patterns themselves (that section may still be
# load-bearing for an actual LaTeX/print product elsewhere in the repo).
!**/🔖️*/
!**/🔖️*/**
*.eledsec[1-9]
*.eledsec[1-9]R
*.eledsec[1-9][0-9]
*.eledsec[1-9][0-9]R
*.eledsec[1-9][0-9][0-9]
*.eledsec[1-9][0-9][0-9]R
